                        "entry_id": "4ddc73eb-80ee-3022-a3a8-d94b0b689664",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not fair, just or right."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85c8bbef-8884-478a-9442-143f3f5db501",
                                "sense_id": "21374221-bcb4-3e24-82ad-1dfdefbb2c6f",
                                "text": "The solution was very unjust."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e45c02e7-b6c3-438a-87ac-2b1ac3a13a3e",
                                "sense_id": "21374221-bcb4-3e24-82ad-1dfdefbb2c6f",
                                "text": "This ſtraunge vnwelcome and vnhappie newes,\nOf theſe vnnaturall Rebels and vniust,\nThat threaten wracke vnto this wretched Land,\nAye me affrights my womans mazed minde,\nBurdens my heart, and interrupts my ſleepe, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90906efa-7ab7-4b73-93cb-fc04288a6cf1",
                                "sense_id": "21374221-bcb4-3e24-82ad-1dfdefbb2c6f",
                                "text": "The rain it raineth all around\nUpon the just and unjust fella;\nBut chiefly on the just because\nThe unjust stole the just’s umbrella."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c994e786-3017-472b-98fe-1559ea66c972",
                                "sense_id": "21374221-bcb4-3e24-82ad-1dfdefbb2c6f",
                                "text": "The Gen Z generation is bringing “good trouble” — a term coined by civil rights activist and politician John Lewis for nonviolent protests against unjust situations — to the “9-9-6 work culture.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
